     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg PO three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.** The maximum daily dose of immediate-release metformin is generally 2,550 mg/day (US labeling), so this is about double the maximum. Metformin also isn't made in a 1700 mg strength, so this may be a transcription or unit error.\n\nSome likely intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum for IR)\n- **1000 mg PO BID with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **1700 mg PO once daily** if an extended-release product was intended (ER is usually dosed once daily with the evening meal, up to 2,000 mg/day)\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose, formulation, and frequency, and I'll enter it. Since this is a 70 kg adult with normal renal and hepatic function, I'd also suggest checking the indication and any recent eGFR, since the appropriate dose depends on those."
      }
     ],
